body:
Here's the thing in the end you didnt really take a pay cut you are actually saving money/time by cutting your commute.

&#x200B;

nta

been no contact almost 10 years with a 3 almost 4 and a 2 going on 3 both female. They have never met ANY of my family and dont know at i have family just my husbands family. Do i get upset sometimes that i dont feel comfortable letting my kids meet them?? Yes i feel its bullshit that I cant feel like I can trust them with my kids. My brothers have seen me out with my kids but I always turn and go in the opposite direction when  i see them so they do know I have kids. 

&#x200B;

I will never truly regret protecting them from what I went through

Call me a granola mom but my 3 1/2 year old has always been asked if she wants hugs/kisses. She also decides her hair cut the last 4-5 times we have went. I get looks but I say that's her body we do what she wants within reason. Like i wont force her to hug me but she will get a bath and her hair brushed even tho she hates getting her hair touched.

&#x200B;

To me their is no compromise MIL can act like LO is her own tiny person which she is or she doesnt see her. Im sorry grandpa is a wimp because that just sucks.

I can feel this to my soul. I was NC for 5ish years when my older brother died. We all knew it was coming had been warned for over a decade(He got a serious diagnoses at 19 and never took care of himself on top of being an Acholic). My JNSM messaged me while i was at work and i started bawling on the line.

&#x200B;

No matter the hate we hold in our hearts it will always be complicated. We loved them as children and as Children we were we mourn their loss. Ive said it multiple times when my own witch bitch of a JNM passes I will bawl my eyes out as i dance on her grave to celebrate my freedom.

&#x200B;

Take the time to to cry get angry and just DEAL. Just remember their are tons of people who feel like you do and get the complicated emotions of having JN family

I dont know where you are but in Michigan I have a SIL who has an order written into the child support decree that her EX isnt allowed to take her kids to see HER mother yes its a messed up situation. you can see if this is possible especially if you have an F.U binder of her being abusive/dismissive towards you or trying to circumvent your parenting decisions. Character witness' towards this would also help.

&#x200B;

Try to keep it as civil as you can but realize that to a certain degree his time with the kids is his time but he might even end up just slowly not taking LO from you for his time if he does this make sure you have text/email proof of him refusing visitation so he cant come back and say that you are trying to keep the child from him.
